 "note": "The Tav: the Vasse Tavern, 44 Queen Street, Busselton, in the old Vasse Hotel (1906, heavily rebuilt 2002-03), on the north-east corner of Queen and Albert Streets. From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), a 2019 street photo and a recent photo of the Queen Street front. Two-storey painted brick hotel, hipped pale roofs behind a cream parapet with VASSE HOTEL lettering, navy ground floor under a deep grey awning on navy posts along Queen Street, and a two-storey navy verandah down the Albert Street side. Signs are plain lettering only, no logos. Metres: x left to right as seen from Queen Street (north to south), y back from the awning edge (east).",
